{{!
    @template local_moderncommerce/components/alert

    Inline status alert — the mc-alert design-system component (Modern Commerce
    design system, component #37). Use it for in-page notices: form-submission
    results, setup warnings, processing hints. For floating, auto-dismissing
    notifications use local_moderncommerce/components/toast instead.

    Variant tints the surface, border, icon, and title; the body text stays
    readable. Colour never carries meaning alone — always pass an icon.

    Context variables:
    * type     - Variant key: success | warning | danger | info | primary | neutral.
                 Defaults to info.
    * icon     - Bootstrap icon class without state, e.g. "bi-check-circle". Optional.
    * title    - Optional bold lead line.
    * message  - Body text. Ignored when a {{$body

    @copyright  2025 Adebare Showemimo | adebareshowemimo@gmail.com | support@agunfoninteractivity.com
    @license    http://www.gnu.org/copyleft/gpl.html GNU GPL v3 or later
}} block is supplied by a parent.
    * role     - ARIA role override. Defaults to "status" (use "alert" for errors).

    Example (context):
    {
        "type": "success",
        "icon": "bi-check-circle",
        "title": "Payment received",
        "message": "Order #1042 marked paid."
    }

}}
<div class="mc-alert mc-alert--{{^type}}info{{/type}}{{type}}" role="{{^role}}status{{/role}}{{role}}">
    {{#icon}}<i class="bi {{icon}} mc-alert__icon" aria-hidden="true"></i>{{/icon}}
    <div class="mc-alert__body">
        {{#title}}<p class="mc-alert__title">{{title}}</p>{{/title}}
        {{$body}}{{message}}{{/body}}
    </div>
</div>
